// One list item's own top-level span: its marker width and checkbox state, and everything that
// belongs to it -- continuation lines, a nested sub-list, loose-list blank lines -- kept as the
// exact raw lines that follow the marker line up to (not including) the next top-level marker line
// (indent 0). Only a line with no leading whitespace can start a new top-level item, so a nested
// item (however it is itself marked) is never mistaken for one (Astra R74 E02). A block with no
