	// stripped) for the consumers that read HTML -- publishing/fragment export, TXT. DOCX is not
	// an HTML consumer: its writer (interchange/docx.mjs) reads the layout comment itself, so
	// stripping it first and handing back CSS only throws the fact away before the writer ever
	// sees it. `keepLayoutData` leaves `data-rapier-image-layout` (width, align AND rotation) and
	// the paragraph's `data-md-align` exactly as the semantic root already carries them, instead
	// of the CSS-only projection, so the one existing layout representation reaches the writer.
